# Seaborn Heatmap Notes

---

## Code

```python
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns
import numpy as np

data = np.random.rand(5,5)

sns.heatmap(
    data,
    annot=True,
    cmap="coolwarm"
)

plt.title("HeatMap")

plt.show()
```

---

# What is a Heatmap?

A **Heatmap** is a chart that uses **colors** to represent values.

```text
High Value
↓
Dark / Strong Color

Low Value
↓
Light Color
```

Instead of reading numbers, you can quickly identify patterns using colors.

---

