# Visual Understanding

Suppose data:

```text
0.10 0.20 0.90

0.30 0.50 0.80

0.15 0.60 0.95
```

Heatmap:

```text
Light   Light   Dark

Light   Medium  Dark

Light   Medium  Dark
```

Higher values get stronger colors.

---

# Real-World Use: Correlation Matrix

Most common use of Heatmap:

```python
corr = df.corr(numeric_only=True)

sns.heatmap(
    corr,
    annot=True,
    cmap="coolwarm"
)

plt.show()
```

---

Example Correlation Matrix

```text
            Age   Salary  Experience

Age          1.00  0.80     0.75

Salary       0.80  1.00     0.92

Experience   0.75  0.92     1.00
```

Heatmap colors help identify:

```text
Strong Relationships

Weak Relationships

Negative Relationships
```

quickly.

